---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
// NOTE TO OWNER: This privacy policy is a strong, plain-language draft based on
// Alberta PIPA / federal PIPEDA principles. Have an Alberta lawyer review it
// (and your screening criteria and consent text) before launch.
const updated = 'June 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How HavenNest collects, uses, protects and retains the personal information you provide.">
  <section class="section container container-narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This policy explains what personal information {site.legalName} collects through this
      website and rental application, why we collect it, and how we protect, use and dispose of it.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose policy">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legalName} ("HavenNest", "we", "us") is an Edmonton, Alberta property builder and
        landlord. We are responsible for the personal information collected through this site and
        our rental application. You can reach us at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you submit a rental application, we may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Identity &amp; contact details (legal name, date of birth, email, phone, current and previous addresses);</li>
        <li>Household information — the people who will live in the unit, their dates of birth, relationship to you, and whether adults (18+) will co-sign the lease;</li>
        <li>Residence and rental history, including landlord references and your reason for moving;</li>
        <li>Employment and income information, from any lawful source;</li>
        <li>Proof of income / pay stubs uploaded with your application;</li>
        <li>Only if your application is shortlisted, and via a separate secure link: a credit report and a government-issued photo ID;</li>
        <li>Pets, vehicles, an emergency contact, and your consents and electronic signature (with a timestamp).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> collect your Social Insurance Number, and we never charge a
        rental application fee. We only collect information that is reasonably required to evaluate
        your application and, if approved, to administer the tenancy.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why we collect it &amp; your consent</h2>
      <p>
        We collect this information to assess your suitability as a tenant and to manage the
        tenancy if you're approved. By submitting the application you consent to this collection
        and use. Before any credit or background check, we ask for your <strong>separate, explicit
        authorization</strong>. You may withdraw consent in writing before a check is performed,
        though this may mean we cannot process your application.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Credit &amp; background checks</h2>
      <p>
        With your authorization, we (or an authorized screening agent) may obtain a consumer credit
        report and verify the information you provide. Your full legal name and date of birth are
        sufficient for this — we do not require your SIN. Where we use a third-party screening
        service, we remain responsible for protecting your information.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How your documents and data are handled</h2>
      <p>
        Uploaded files are transmitted over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection and stored in a private,
        access-restricted location; we generate only short-lived links for authorized review and
        never publish your documents. Your application is delivered securely to HavenNest. We apply
        consistent screening criteria to every applicant and do not make decisions based on
        protected characteristics under the <em>Alberta Human Rights Act</em> (including source of
        income, family status, or similar grounds).
      </p>

      <h2>6. Service providers &amp; cross-border processing</h2>
      <p>
        We use reputable infrastructure providers (including Cloudflare for hosting, security,
        storage and email delivery, and GitHub for site hosting) to operate this site and process
        applications. Some of these providers may store or process data on servers located outside
        Alberta or Canada, where it may be subject to the laws of those jurisdictions. We take
        reasonable steps to ensure our providers protect your information.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Retention &amp; secure destruction</h2>
      <p>
        We keep applicant information only as long as reasonably necessary. If your application is
        not successful, we securely destroy your application and supporting documents (such as your
        credit report, proof of income and any ID image) within a reasonable period once they are
        no longer needed. If you become a tenant, we retain the information needed to administer
        your tenancy for as long as required.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access to, or correction of, the personal information we hold about you, and
        you may ask questions about how it is handled. Contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> and we will respond as
        required under Alberta's <em>Personal Information Protection Act</em> (PIPA) and, where
        applicable, the federal <em>Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act</em>
        (PIPEDA).
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date above reflects the most
        recent revision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .muted {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    margin-top: -0.5rem;
  }
  .policy {
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }
</style>
